{{also|quorn}}
==English==

===Etymology===
Shortened from earlier {{m|en|Quorndon}}, from {{inh|en|ang|cweorndun}}, from {{af|ang|cweorn|t1=millstone; quern|dun|t2=hill|nocat=1}}. The fox hunt, the meat substitute<ref>''Oxford Dictionary of English'' (2010), page 1459</ref><ref>{{R:Lexico}}</ref> and the town in Australia are named after the village in Leicestershire.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/kwɔːn/}}
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/k(w)ɔɹn/}}
* {{audio|en|en-uk-Quorn.ogg|Audio (UK)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɔː(ɹ)n|s=1}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{lb|en|with "the"}} A famous [[fox hunt]] (one of the world's oldest, established in 1696) in [[Leicestershire]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1902|author=John Buchan|title=The Watcher by the Threshold
|passage=The House of More has a pretty Georgian paneling through most of the rooms, but in the dining room the walls are level and painted a dull stone color. {{...}} Some photographs of the '''Quorn''' hung over the mantelpiece, and five or six drab ancestors filled up the remaining space.}}
#* {{RQ:Wodehouse Jeeves in the Offing|chapter=XII|passage=I've never hunted myself, but I understand that half the battle is being able to make noises like some jungle animal with dyspepsia, and I believe that Aunt Dahlia in her prime could lift fellow-members of the '''Quorn''' and Pytchley out of their saddles with a single yip, though separated from them by two ploughed fields and a spinney.}}
# {{place|en|village/and/civil parish|(formerly ''[[Quorndon]]'') in|dist/Charnwood|co/Leicestershire|cc/England}} {{q|[[OS]] grid ref SK5616}}.
# {{place|en|town|s/South Australia}}.
# A [[mycoprotein]]-based [[food]] [[product]] used as a [[substitute]] for [[meat]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2004|author=J. L. Clarke; Mary Dougherty Riley; Veronica Dougherty|title=OCR National Certificate in Health and Social Care: Level 2|page=384
|passage=It is now easier for a vegetarian to eat sufficient protein because of products such as '''Quorn''', tofu and textured vegetable protein.}}
#* {{quote-web |en |date=2006-10-20 |author=Julian Dibbell |title=The Ultra-Extreme Calorie Restriction Diet Test |work=New York Magazine |url=http://nymag.com/news/features/23169/ 
|passage=April brings the main course: a medley of asparagus tips, shiitake mushrooms, and the featured ingredient, an unlikely hybrid of life-giving wholesomeness and bio-industrial hubris known as '''Quorn'''.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2011|author=Rosemary Conley|title=Rosemary Conley's Amazing Inch Loss Plan|page=257|passage=For a vegetarian option, use '''Quorn''' pieces instead of prawns.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=July 21 2023|author=Billie Schwab Dunn|titleurl=https://www.dailystar.co.uk/real-life/i-tried-wetherspoons-food-first-30518473|title=I Tried Wetherspoons Food for the First Time-I Feared I'd Get Scurvy...|journal=w:Daily Star
|passage=I opted for the vegan breakfast (£4.57), which comes with two '''Quorn''' sausages, baked beans, two hash browns, mushroom, tomato, a slice of toast and a vegan spread.}}

